Subject: Default to system allocator and fix strcase pointer provenance under Fil-C
Policy-Class: P4-Audit
Rationale: Zend's 2 MiB chunk allocator hides intra-chunk overflows and UAF between PHP values; default USE_ZEND_ALLOC=0 under __FILC__ so every value gets its own capability, and compute res offsets from res instead of source in zend_str_tolower_dup_ex()/zend_string_tolower_ex().
Upstream-Status: Fil-C-Specific (strcase offset fix is upstreamable)
Fil-C-Origin-Commits: 18e0199cef6c30fc815442c0dd3f9d97fae3702a
Origin-Kind: filc-upstream
Origin-Project: pizlonator/fil-c
Origin-Commit: 18e0199cef6c30fc815442c0dd3f9d97fae3702a
Origin-URL: https://github.com/pizlonator/fil-c/commit/18e0199cef6c30fc815442c0dd3f9d97fae3702a

--- a/Zend/zend_alloc.c
+++ b/Zend/zend_alloc.c
@@ -2708,7 +2708,13 @@
 
 #if ZEND_MM_CUSTOM
 	tmp = getenv("USE_ZEND_ALLOC");
+#ifdef __FILC__
+	/* Default to system malloc so every PHP value gets its own capability.
+	 * Set USE_ZEND_ALLOC=1 to opt into Zend's chunk allocator. */
+	if (!tmp || !zend_atoi(tmp, 0)) {
+#else
 	if (tmp && !zend_atoi(tmp, 0)) {
+#endif
 		alloc_globals->mm_heap = malloc(sizeof(zend_mm_heap));
 		memset(alloc_globals->mm_heap, 0, sizeof(zend_mm_heap));
 		alloc_globals->mm_heap->use_custom_heap = ZEND_MM_CUSTOM_HEAP_STD;
